{"_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"content": "Sally in Russia", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "A Long History", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 11, "type": "position"}, {"content": "stub", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 2, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "A2.2", "type": "level"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"content": "Accurately use information about methods of communication and communication technology in common social situations.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": "Understands important information and aspects of attitude and intention in spoken situations in English on a range of common communicative topics related to this level.", "type": "secondary_1"}, {"content": "Instructions: Move the words from the box to correctly complete the sentences. Record yourself saying the sentences aloud. Compare yourself to the audio. ", "type": "secondary_2"}, {"content": "Understands important information and aspects of attitude and intention in spoken situations in English on a range of common communicative topics related to this level.", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": "Understands important information and aspects of attitude and intention in spoken situations in English on a range of common communicative topics related to this level.", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": "Identifies the expressions and vocabulary necessary for the description of places of work and jobs in common written and spoken situations. ", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": "Identifies the expressions and vocabulary necessary for the description of places of work and jobs in common written and spoken situations.", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": "Understands important information and aspects of attitude and intention in spoken situations in English on a range of common communicative topics related to this level.", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": "Understands important information and aspects of attitude and intention in spoken situations in English on a range of common communicative topics related to this level.", "type": "secondary_8"}]}, {"content": "engenn5le02ob11re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Rooms and Objects", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "When you visit old homes and palaces, guides talk about the rooms and objects in them. Here are some words you could hear:", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "There were 500 people in the Grand Hall dancing.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "The chandelier has thousands of tiny crystals hanging from it.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":5,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Room or Object\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Meaning\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"gallery\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"large open room often with artwork in it\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"chamber\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"a room for a particular purpose\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"chandelier\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"ornate light hanging from the ceiling\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"rooms\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"area where people lived and worked\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" instruction_table_background intro_table_border\"}", "type": "table"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "The Simple Past Tense", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You use the Simple Past tense to talk about events that are finished.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "The guide took me to the Great Hall.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "The gold woodwork flashed in the light.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Simple Past tense verbs can be regular or irregular.</br> Regular past tense verbs end in <span class=\"italic\">-ed</span> or <span class=\"italic\">-ied</span>. (<span class=\"italic\">worked, visited, danced, studied</span>)<br/><br/>Irregular verbs have significant changes in their form. Make sure you practice these changes for the most common verbs (have > had; go > went; see > saw, etc.). <br/><br/> For questions in the past, you use the auxiliary <span class=\"italic\">did</span>.<br/>  <span class=\"italic\">Did</span> is the past form of <span class=\"italic\">to do</span>. <br/><br/> <span class=\"strong\">REMEMBER</span>: When you use the auxiliary verb in past, the principal verb is in the basic form. Do not conjugate the principal verb in questions. (<span class=\"italic\">e.g. <span class=\"strong\">Did</span> you <span class=\"strong\">visit</span> the Great Hall? <span class=\"strong\">Did</span> you <span class=\"strong\">see</span> the pictures of the Kremlin Gallery?</span>)", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":8,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Verb\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Simple Past Tense\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"to dance\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"danced\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"to talk\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"talked\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"to laugh\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"laughed\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"to protect\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"protected\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"to be\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"was\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"to make\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"made\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"to think\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"thought\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" instruction_table_background intro_table_border\"}", "type": "table"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to protect", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to keep someone or something from harm", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: They put up a wall to protect the King's palace. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn5le02ob11aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": "These are words you use to talk about Russia's history.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "gilded", "type": "name"}, {"content": "painted with a thin layer of real gold ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: The doors of the palace are gilded. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn5le02ob11aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "crystal", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a transparent rock that looks like ice ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: The lights have crystals hanging from them. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn5le02ob11aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "column", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a tall support for a building ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: The Bolshoi Theater has a row of columns in front. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn5le02ob11aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "ballerina ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "someone who dances in the ballet ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: The ballerina danced in Swan Lake. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn5le02ob11aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "slipper", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a thin indoor shoe", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: He gave her pink ballet slippers to wear. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn5le02ob11aud06", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "coronation", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a ceremony where a person  is made king or queen", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: People went to the Kremlin after a coronation.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn5le02ob11aud07", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "chamber ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a room or space for a specific purpose", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: The tsars were buried in that chamber. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn5le02ob11aud08", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "tzar/tsar ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a Russian emperor ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: This is where the Russian tsars lived.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn5le02ob11aud09", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"content": "Find out why the place is important.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Write down what happened there.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Find out when people can visit the place.  ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Find out how much it costs to go in.  ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Read your sentences to a partner.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Listen to your partner's  sentences.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"content": "I research a historical house or building.", "type": "text"}, {"conten